+## Revision 1.4.48 — dependency-aware planning and correction (PROPOSED)
+
+Extend FR-003/009/027–035/101–105/117–124, R-ASE-09/13/19/32/38–42 and existing T-422/T-455/T-459/T-461. Canonical 03 owns the technical contract, 04 supported adapters and 05 proof. This refines the v1.4.46/47 controls; it creates no new graph store, runtime, endpoint, status family or approval authority. The “Loops and Graphs” source in canonical 00 is design input, not runtime or effectiveness evidence.
+
+- **Two meanings of graph.** The application/assurance graph expresses attributed source relationships, obligations, expected behavior and evidence. A task's execution dependency graph expresses which bounded work may proceed, its prerequisites and checks. The latter may reference exact records from the former; neither structure establishes the other's truth or completion. A Model Studio path proposal is not an agent execution plan or proof that target actions ran.
+- **Checks before generation.** Before generating a normative artifact or attempting an effect, establish the intended outcome, independent expected basis, required/forbidden effects, discriminating observations and their permitted observer. A generator cannot approve its own oracle. Missing or conflicting authority creates a scoped clarification/investigation task; safe evidence gathering and unrelated work remain possible without inventing an expected result or forcing model-first development. Preserve the check/rubric revision when subsequent work changes it.
+- **Dependencies beyond values.** Planning and independent review consider consumed outputs plus actual shared resource/record, authority/policy/Skill, state/fixture, ordering and external-effect dependencies. Each material prerequisite has a typed meaning, exact known basis, scope and evidence/unknowns under the existing task/change owner. Two tasks that exchange no value can still conflict through one test account, object or permission. Parallelism requires supported independence; an absent edge is not proof of it. Incomplete discovery limits the claim to the inspected frontier.
+- **Local correction, complete revalidation.** A failed check identifies the affected candidate and suspected mechanism. Preserve its original output/evidence, propose a scoped successor and re-evaluate affected downstream consumers and shared prerequisites on the new basis. Retain an unaffected check only when its recorded inputs, authority, state/resource conditions and validity remain justified; missing dependency evidence cannot authorize a clean result. The integrated check over the current dependency-closed selected work remains required before any completion/release recommendation. Successful local checks or clean text merges do not establish combined business correctness, publication or release. Historical accepted artifacts and results change only through their native reviewed correction paths.
+- **Bounded attempts with progress.** Classify the observed failure before retry: transient tool/transport issue, invalid input, stale basis, unmet permission, unknown external outcome, failed expectation or unresolved authority need different recovery. Choose retry, targeted evidence, revised plan, wait, clarification or stop using the admitted step/time/cost limits, remaining authorization and evidence of progress. No universal retry count is selected. Repeated unchanged attempts cannot establish progress; uncertain effects require receipt reconciliation before another mutation. Preserve linked attempts and the reason for stopping without relabeling a budget limit as product success.
+- **Learn within scope and authority.** A supported failure/correction may produce a reviewed planning constraint or Skill candidate with its cause, applicability, provenance, counterexample and invalidation/review trigger. A transient failure or one project's rule does not become a permanent universal instruction. Changed conditions require reassessment; rejecting a bad hypothesis is valid learning. Human decisions occur where actual authority is needed—before a reserved action or consequential interpretation as well as at final review. Existing authorized routine decisions continue without ritual approval; agent consensus cannot replace the missing authority.
+
+Acceptance extends existing proof owners: a locally repaired output invalidates an affected dependent check while an evidenced independent check remains reusable; independent-looking tasks sharing mutable state are coordinated; a stale grant blocks only its dependent action; and individually passing parts with an inconsistent combined effect fail the integrated check. Include valid alternate plans, unresolved dependencies, no-progress retries and interrupted uncertain effects. A proposed read-only demonstration may compare recorded plan/check revisions and proposed dispositions without generation, native writes or dispatch. It is **NOT RUN** and cannot establish scheduling, recovery, improved QA or live approval enforcement.
+
+## Revision 1.4.49 — general optional contributions
+
+**FR-125 — General-purpose plugin capability (PROPOSED / BACKLOG).** Permit optional, versioned contributions to Tesbo through explicit host contracts while preserving the usable core QA workflow and native authority. Obsidian is one possible source connector. Do not infer first-delivery priority, a mandatory local application, an open marketplace or arbitrary executable/UI admission from that example. The admitted profile set is an accountable product decision. FR-058 remains the narrower execution-agent contract.
+
+The requirement has these separately verifiable obligations:
+
+- **Purpose and effects:** describe the user outcome and actual reads, writes, execution, external transmission and UI contributions. A label such as analysis or read-only does not override actual effects. Compare a built-in/configuration/manual alternative before requiring a plugin.
+- **Distinct facts:** keep package identity and verified version/digest, contribution identity, account connection, workspace/project binding, enabled state, effective grant, compatibility and observed health separate. Installing or enabling a package does not grant target access, activate a Skill or prove operational readiness.
+- **Native ownership:** connectors use integration/knowledge owners; executors use Tasks/attempts/Runs/evidence; method packs use exact-version Skills review and separate activation; reports read permitted native facts; other admitted contributions name their owning service. A contribution cannot independently confer approval, manufacture test outcomes or become another authoritative store for the same fact. A permitted human action through an admitted UI still uses the existing native approval owner and exact reviewed basis.
+- **Composition:** namespace contributions; define whether an extension point accepts one provider, several independent providers or an explicitly ordered composition. Reject ambiguous collisions and unsupported dependencies without silent last-loaded-wins behavior or partially active contributions.
+- **Lifecycle:** qualify install/admit, connect, enable, invoke, update, permission change, disable, revoke and remove for the selected profile. Validate transitive dependencies and exact-version compatibility; preserve valid unrelated work. A package downgrade does not establish data/schema rollback. Removal and data purge are separate authorized operations.
+- **Trust and operation:** derive the required boundary from actual code, data, principals and effects. A manifest, signature, trusted publisher, process or iframe alone is not proof of safe execution or tenant isolation. Reuse revisions 1.4.47–48 for current authority, fencing, resource budgets, independent evidence and stopping. Keep the plugin-free core usable when an optional contribution is absent, refused or fails.
+- **Usability and recovery:** make effects, scope, permission changes, dependency impact, retained data, unsupported behavior and the available next action understandable to the affected actor. An unknown write must remain unknown until reconciled with the native owner.
+- **Evidence:** qualify the distributed artifact and actual native consumer; preserve source versions, operation/attempt identity, permitted evidence and original outcomes. Documentation review, source inspection, installation, invocation and verified effects are separate claims.
+
+**Traceability and authority.** Canonical 03/04 define the contract boundaries; AC-094 in canonical 05 defines acceptance. T-462 qualifies the proposed design without activating it. Reuse existing Requirements, Cases, Runs, Policies, Manuals and Tasks where their obligations match; the numerical historical inventories retain their original scope. FR-125 is one new proposed specification identity, not an official native Requirement or implementation result.
