+## Revision 1.4.48 — understand the plan, repair the affected work and review the result (PROPOSED)
+
+Extend WF-03/WF-05/WF-19–24, ASER-UX01–03 and the existing Agents task detail, Zyra proposal review, Change Workspace and native Run/evidence views. These are proposed interactions under existing states and permissions; no execution scheduler or new graph screen is asserted. Keep v1.4.47 delegation, waiting, containment and recovery controls. A list/table is sufficient; an optional graph renders the same authorized facts.
+
+1. **See the objective and check first.** The task shows the requested outcome, source/requirement and Skill revisions, independent acceptance/check basis, allowed effects and evidence still needed. Separate the application's obligation/trace links from the work's prerequisite sequence. A proposed check is labeled as such; a plan edge, generated case or green structural validator never displays as an executed assertion. When a business expectation is unsettled, show the affected question, known alternatives, accountable decision owner and safe work that can continue.
+2. **Understand what can proceed.** Explain each material dependency in the user's terms: waiting for a specific result, shared account/record or environment state, current permission/decision, or an uncertain prior effect. Link to its exact authorized basis. Show why apparently independent work must wait and which work is genuinely unaffected; unknown or inaccessible dependencies remain explicitly incomplete without leaking hidden records or counts. Starting an existing-item check must not silently create a second batch, regenerate content or dispatch a runner.
