+
+### Trust, availability and observability
+
+Apply 1.4.47's credential custody, actual effect authorization, isolation, egress, independent evidence and stopping contracts, and 1.4.48's resource/dependency controls. Trusted compiled host code and untrusted third-party execution have different threat models. A manifest, package signature, separate process or browser sandbox label alone proves none of the required hostile-code boundaries. Keep host session cookies/tokens and ambient headers out of plugin proxies; use explicitly scoped credentials through the existing owner and verify actual outbound requests.
